From: cline <cline@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 21:16:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] [qwen38] tokenize-v1-route

Serve /tokenize and /detokenize under /v1 as well as at the root.

Every OpenAI SDK client (and most gateways) points base_url at a URL ending
in /v1 and resolves every endpoint relative to it, so the root-only routes
were a genuine 404 for them: the tokenization endpoints were unusable from
stock clients. The router is now included twice, once as-is and once with
prefix="/v1"; FastAPI derives each route's operation id from name + path +
method, so the two mounts carry distinct ids (tokenize_tokenize_post /
tokenize_v1_tokenize_post) and the OpenAPI schema stays valid.
---
 vllm/entrypoints/serve/tokenize/api_router.py | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vllm/entrypoints/serve/tokenize/api_router.py b/vllm/entrypoints/serve/tokenize/api_router.py
index 9695e6c..67a16b1 100644
--- a/vllm/entrypoints/serve/tokenize/api_router.py
+++ b/vllm/entrypoints/serve/tokenize/api_router.py
@@ -107,3 +107,10 @@ def attach_router(app: FastAPI):
             )
 
     app.include_router(router)
+    # Also under /v1: OpenAI SDK clients and most gateways point base_url at
+    # a URL ending in /v1 and resolve every endpoint relative to it, so the
+    # root-only routes were a genuine 404 for them. FastAPI derives a route's
+    # operation id from name + path + method, so the two mounts carry
+    # distinct ids (tokenize_tokenize_post / tokenize_v1_tokenize_post) and
+    # the OpenAPI schema stays valid.
+    app.include_router(router, prefix="/v1")
